msgid "Dev Services for Elasticsearch"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If any Elasticsearch-related extension is present (e.g. `quarkus-"
"elasticsearch-rest-client` or `quarkus-hibernate-search-orm-elasticsearch`),\n"
"Dev Services for Elasticsearch automatically starts an Elasticsearch server "
"in dev mode and when running tests.\n"
"So, you don't have to start a server manually.\n"
"The application is configured automatically."
msgstr ""

msgid "Enabling / Disabling Dev Services for Elasticsearch"
msgstr ""

msgid "Dev Services for Elasticsearch is automatically enabled unless:"
msgstr ""

msgid "`quarkus.devservices.enabled` is set to `false`."
msgstr ""

msgid "`quarkus.elasticsearch.devservices.enabled` is set to `false`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"the hosts property is configured, depending on the extension used it can be:"
msgstr ""

msgid "`quarkus.elasticsearch.hosts`"
msgstr ""

msgid "`quarkus.hibernate-search-orm.elasticsearch.hosts`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Dev Services for Elasticsearch relies on Docker to start the server.\n"
"If your environment does not support Docker, you will need to start the "
"server manually, or connect to an already running server."
msgstr ""

msgid "Shared Elasticsearch"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Sometimes you need to share the server between applications.\n"
"Dev Services for Elasticsearch implements a _service discovery_ mechanism "
"for your multiple Quarkus applications running in _dev_ mode to share a "
"single server."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you need multiple (shared) servers, you can configure the `quarkus."
"elasticsearch.devservices.service-name` attribute and indicate the server "
"name.\n"
"It looks for a container with the same value, or starts a new one if none "
"can be found.\n"
"The default service name is `elasticsearch`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Sharing is enabled by default in dev mode, but disabled in test mode.\n"
"You can disable the sharing with `quarkus.elasticsearch.devservices.shared="
"false`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Setting the port"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"By default, Dev Services for Elasticsearch picks a random port and "
"configures the application.\n"
"You can set the port by configuring the `quarkus.elasticsearch.devservices."
"port` property."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Note that the Elasticsearch hosts property is automatically configured with "
"the chosen port."
msgstr ""

msgid "Configuring the image"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Dev Services for Elasticsearch only support Elasticsearch based images, "
"OpenSearch is not supported at the moment."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you need to use a different image than the default one you can configure "
"it via:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Current limitations"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Currently, only the default backend for Hibernate Search Elasticsearch is "
"supported, because Dev Services for Elasticsearch can only start one "
"Elasticsearch container."
msgstr ""

